<!--Post: 713--><!--Time: 1092062173-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST713"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 09, 2004 - 7:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Flytodeb: <BR> <BR>And the sources are excellent ones! Also, it&#39;s not a dissertation; the sources at the bottom of the article are certainly sufficient. I&#39;ve a pet peeve <BR>about something which is presented as scholarly but doesn&#39;t use footnotes naming the exact title, author and page number.  <BR> <BR>Anything which might engender discussion is important, particularly when the powers-that-be <BR>in Wichita furnish so little information. <BR>A serious thank you for posting the article; you provide much help and it&#39;s appreciated. <BR> I remember your screen name from one of the other BTK boards in I think March or April and I enjoyed your posts there, too. Have a great day and let&#39;s catch this critter!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 713-->
<!--Post: 816--><!--Time: 1092877485-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST816"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 18, 2004 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, the other article was short. Have you read this 22 page article called &#34;Signature Killers&#34; that is purple font on black background? I copied it and pasted it into my word processor, changed the font to black and made it the size that was easiest for me to read. For those of you who are picky, you can edit the typos out of your copy. haha  <BR> <BR>If this has been posted on another thread in this forum, then sorry. Here it is again. lol <BR>-Deb <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.angelfire.com/sc3/cjrp/signature.html" target=_top>http://www.angelfire.com/sc3/cjrp/signature.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 816-->
<!--Post: 952--><!--Time: 1093871771-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST952"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 30, 2004 - 6:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom:  I read Pat Brown&#39;s profile of BTK. Though he has killed in a serial fashion, she feels that he is pretending to be a compulsively driven serial killer in the traditional sense.  A sadist to be sure but otherwise, he is deliberately misleading everyone. If that is true, all bets are off in trying to profile, analyze, predict, and locate this person. That may account for the lack of progress in the case. God forbid, the police know who he is and they are hesitant to point a finger at him because of position or family/personal power or prestige. He could be married and his killing dates correspond, not to his schedule, but times when his spouse/significant other&#40;s&#41; was out of town, state, etc. If the death of the Oteros was indeed a &#39;hit&#39; of sorts against Joe Otero, as Ms. Brown thinks, that is where the police should be looking. Could he have done some of the other killings to cover the Otero deaths and feed his sadistic nature at the same time? Wouldn&#39;t it be interesting if he was in a witness protection program with the feds covering his tracks inadvertently. Just brainstorming. What better place to hide than Kansas. <BR> <BR>What do you think? Could we all be wee weeing in the wind?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 952-->
<!--Post: 1139--><!--Time: 1097425529-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1139"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wolfgang<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wolfgang<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, October 10, 2004 - 9:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK is a sadomasochist and the only way he will truly be satisfied and contented would be to perfect the art of OBE so that he could inflicted pain and pleasure upon himself at the same time. <BR>Twice the fun from One. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1139-->
<!--Post: 1242--><!--Time: 1097883127-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1242"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 4:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Heres my 2 quarters: <BR> <BR>First I personally like &#40;swa&#41; profile suggestion. <BR>This is what I feel BTK&#39;s profile might be.  First he is very quiet, sickly smart, manager, long time employee,teacher of IT field, very aware of internet protocols.  Very aware of the dangers of ip addresses, mac addresses, default gateways, and subnet masks. Whatsmore most IT professionals such as TV repairmen, Computer techs &#40;geeks&#41;, usually care some sort of black bag, for things such as tools, multi-meters, and various other electronic type equipment.  Are these guys friendly when they come out to your home?  You bet they are, they are very well paid and trusted?  I feel that is a short person say 5&#39;7&#34; tops, and he does&#39;nt hate women, but because of his size, wants to feel in control?  As for the puzzles, well computer language is in binary, there for is a series of 0110010110, which in itself is a puzzle.  You can use the powers of X or &#40;10&#41; to figure them out, which is a form of math.  Maybe this is the X, the WPD is talking about?  I feel that BTK is a ordinary individual with a dark side, and is a very respected, teacher, boss, manager, of what ever type of work he does.  In reference to the word &#34;dude,&#34;  well I think it might be his way of feeling young after all these years?  That&#39;s my story and I&#39;m stickin to it. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1242-->
<!--Post: 1244--><!--Time: 1097891147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1244"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 6:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s another great link with reguards to BTK&#39;s profile. <BR> <BR>  <a href="http://crime.about.com/gi/dynamic/offsite.htm?zi=1/XJ&amp;sdn=crime&amp;zu=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.kansas.com%2Fmld%2Fkansas%2Fnews%2Fspecial_packages%2Fbtk%2F8294875.htm" target=_top>http://crime.about.com/gi/dynamic/offsite.htm?zi=1 /XJ&amp;sdn=crime&amp;zu=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.kansas.com%2Fmld %2Fkansas%2Fnews%2Fspecial_packages%2Fbtk%2F829487 5.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1244-->
<!--Post: 1260--><!--Time: 1098098589-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1260"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, October 18, 2004 - 4:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with some of the characteristics and disagree with others of the profile. The BTK Strangler has remained in Wichita, Kansas for the last thirty years living with a family and maintaining a facade of respectability to conceal his psychopathic desires. He does not have a criminal record. He is a graduate with a degree in the physical sciences or engineering. He may have studied some literature classes at college and is familiar with Wichita State University. It could be his alma mater. <BR> <BR>It seems unlikely that he will communicate electronically. The reference to the Crime Library.com chapter titles is an attempt to create the impression the BTK Strangler is omnipresent and possibly omnipotent and is determined to craft his own biography and document his achievements rather than read the narrative of an individual who he considers lacks insight and knowledge of him. <BR> <BR>He will continue to communicate with the media and police by claiming responsibility for unsolved murders. This will involve supplying them with photographs of trophies collected from the victim or illustrations of the crime scene. <BR> <BR>The desire to communicate is motivated by the psychopathic traits to control and manipulate a docile population. He most probably ceased communication in the late 1970s based on the fear he may be captured.He is aware that most of the population have forgotten his threat and the police have concentrated on other cases during the last 25 years. Increased leisure time has allowed him to devote time and energy to his old pursuit. <BR> <BR>He craves attention and recognition as a successful serial murderer. He enjoys visiting websites dedicated to serial murder and reading articles on his achievements. He seems reluctant to participate in a forum or respond to a challenge. It undermines his desire to dominate and control. <BR> <BR>Its highly unlikely the BTK Strangler will ever be apprehended. He is aware he possesses superior intelligence and enjoys taunting the police, media and public with his accomplishments. Most importantly, he enjoys freedom.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1260-->
<!--Post: 1470--><!--Time: 1101861373-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1470"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m quite curious what Mike Kelleher thinks about BTK&#39;s <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/113004.html"> <b>recent claims</b></a>...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1470-->
<!--Post: 1477--><!--Time: 1101862624-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Tom: <BR> <BR>Today&#39;s press release is very interesting. Probably the most interesting aspect is what was NOT released to the public. The holdbacks would be fascinating and probably revealing. Most of the claims make sense to me, although not all of them. For example, the train/railroad connection may not be as it was portrayed in the press release. This item may be borrowed, or BTK may have used it for other purposes that we don&#39;t know since we don&#39;t know the context in which it was used. Remember that he claimed that his mother raised him without his father. Something doesn&#39;t make complete sense here. My instincts tell me that this has some significance but not necessarily as it was portrayed in the release. <BR> <BR>I also have some problems with his alleged career. This was probably something he worked at for a while but not for a long period of time, in my opinion. Also, why was there no mention of a domestic life? Is this a holdback? It would be common for a writer like BTK to link his career and his domestic life when telling his story. Where is the domestic part of his story? <BR> <BR>Anyway, it&#39;s hard to say right now. I need to think about it some more and watch the wires for what comes down. All in all, I&#39;m still happy with my original profile, at least in comparison with what we learned today. I&#39;m also fairly convinced that a good deal of the press release is probably some version of the truth from BTK&#39;s standpoint, although I can&#39;t help but believe that it has been sanitized and directed by authorities for later, legal purposes. <BR> <BR>As I mentioned in my original profile, I think the time is near for BTK to come forward, one way or the other. If, in fact, the investigators have such a good deal of information, they should be able to narrow their suspects to a small number. One has to wonder why, then, are they seeking help from the public? Perhaps they were working on some poor theories for many years and now have to do some serious re-thinking. <BR> <BR>Hopefully, we&#39;re all getting close to closing this case down, once and for all. <BR> <BR>Mike <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1477-->
<!--Post: 1479--><!--Time: 1101864479-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1479"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 5:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree abput the context being important. <BR> <BR>&#34;Since last March, BTK has sent numerous communications to the media and the police. In these letters he has provided certain background information about himself which he claims is accurate. Based upon a review of that information, the following facts about BTK are being made available to the public in hopes of identifying BTK&#34; <BR> <BR>It sounds like they are releasing bits and pieces of info gleaned from multiple letters.  Who knows how much is even in his own words. Some of it may even be based on assumption or lateral thinking/interpretations.   <BR> <BR>Statements such as: <BR> <BR>&#34;He has a basic knowledge of photography and the ability to develop and print pictures.&#34; <BR> <BR>make me wonder the context in which it was presented.  Did he say he took pictures of the crime scenes and developed them in his home dark room?  Or did he say he worked in a photo lab thereby having the skills and access to the equipment? <BR> <BR>Either scenario could have resulted in the rather generic statement above.  I doubt, in the narrative, he would say &#34;I have a basic knowledge of photography and the ability to develop and print pictures.&#34; <BR> <BR>Sorry this has gotten a bit long.  I really think the narrative is very important, as far as context and nuance.   <BR> <BR>What we have here is a laundry list that has more than likely been simplified, rephrased, taken out of context and who knows what else. <BR> <BR>We also have the list that is preface by &#34;Based on the investigation we believe...&#34; <BR>This is the area where they mention WSU and PJ Wyatt.  That info is not claimed to come directly from BTK.   <BR> <BR>Lastly, nowhere was it claimed that he was born in Wichita, nor when he lived there.  Maybe his cousin moved to Missouri from Colorado. Cousins do not always reside in the same state.  Again, we are certainly missing a lot here. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1479-->
<!--Post: 1482--><!--Time: 1101869635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1482"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 6:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->By quite a coincidence I visited all the known BTK crime scenes on Monday the 29, then a couple of hours later saw some of the places I had just visited on the evening news!  My wife and I were visiting her hometown of Winfield, about 40 miles from Wichita.  For what it is worth regarding the fascination with railroads bit, having been there just yesterday several of the crime scenes are near railroad tracks, including S. Hydraulic st. and the UPS drop box on Kansas st.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1482-->
<!--Post: 1484--><!--Time: 1101870340-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 7:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>If</i> BTK ws born in 1939, the typical profile says he likely would have started killing in the late 1950s/early 1960s. In other words, long before the Otero murders of 1974. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1484-->
<!--Post: 1537--><!--Time: 1101954547-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1537"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:mrsdochash@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chash<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chash<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 01, 2004 - 6:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO I believe he has killed add&#39;l victims other than what we know of.  <BR>Juno, as far as the photgraphy experince,  he has sent to the media copies of pics of the murdered victims that were NOT taken by police. <BR>As a resident of wichita..I believe he is very familiar and/or lives somewhere in the north central part of town.   <BR>1. That is the major area of town where all the trains enter/leave the city. <BR>2. The north part of wichita is also considered the hispanic community. &#40;His so called petra girlfriend &amp; the Oteros are hispanic&#41; <BR>Those are just my thoughts       <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1537-->
<!--Post: 1589--><!--Time: 1102114333-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1589"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 03, 2004 - 2:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The portrait crafted by the BTK Strangler is an attempt to manipulate and control the police and public. Some of the characteristics would be based on fact and others based on fantasy or lies. The interest in photography and living near railways could be legitimate. Personal details, such as the year he was born or his relationship with a girlfriend could be false. I presume he found Petra attractive and viewed her from a distance. She may have rejected his attention. The BTK Strangler may have incorporated her into his fantasies. <BR> <BR>Any information provided by a serial murderer to the police has to be scrutinized, particularly a self portrait. The self portrait will contain details he wants the police and public to believe. It will ignore details not corresponding with the personality traits or facts he wants projected to the police and public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1589-->
<!--Post: 1643--><!--Time: 1102487300-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 07, 2004 - 10:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I quite agree, Ivy_Leaguer. Except that the release seems more crafted by law enforcement than by BTK. I wonder if the police are in essence <BR>saying &#34;We&#39;d like <i>specific</i> information from the public. Please, no more generalized, vague stories about some uncle or man down the street who behaved in a strange fashion during the BTK killing years?&#34; <BR> <BR>I also wonder if the police are specifically asking BTK for more information. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1643-->
<!--Post: 1679--><!--Time: 1102589193-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1679"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 2:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The profile of the BTK Strangler released by Wichita police seems to contradict witness accounts of the unknown suspect. Kathryn Bright&#39;s brother, Kevin provided statements describing the BTK Strangler as a white male approximately 25 years of age in 1974. A postal employee stated she spoke to the unknown suspect in June 1979. He sent a letter to KAKE-TV. She described him as a white male approximately 30 years of age. <BR> <BR>Witness accounts suggest the BTK Strangler was most probably born in the late 1940s or early 1950s. I presume he studied at Wichita State University in the mid 1970s. He asked Kevin Bright, &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the University?&#34; Bright did not attend university. The BTK Strangler believes he possesses superior intelligence and would find it difficult to prevent this piece of information from being known. <BR> <BR>I do not believe his father died in World War II. Based on the assumption he was born in the late 1940s or early 1950s it would be impossible. I suggest his father may have died in the Korean War &#40;1950 - 1953&#41; or the Vietnam War. Its difficult to determine the relationship with his mother or grandfather. I would like to suggest he would not have appreciated his mother marrying another man. It could have sown the seeds for hating his mother and attempting to resolve his oedipal dilemma by murdering in adulthood. His hatred for his mother and possible rejection by other women in his life can be observed by masturbating at the crime scene and the brutality of the murders. Multiple stab wounds, such as Kathryn Bright&#39;s murder implies anger and rage. He could be punishing his mother by murdering other women.    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1679-->
<!--Post: 1699--><!--Time: 1102628016-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1699"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 1:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR>    Would you read anything into the fact that BTK&#39;s first letter back had a stamp depticting a train, in relation to his claims about railroads etc. <BR>If for example &#40;as you suggest&#41; police may be reworking some poor theories, would it not suggest that he was following up with this &#34;theme&#34;. <BR>On the other hand, if this is new information would it not suggest he was reinforcing this connection. Perhaps it&#39;s true or it&#39;s something he put some thought into or perhaps it&#39;s just a coincidence!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1699-->
<!--Post: 1700--><!--Time: 1102628386-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1700"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 1:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OOPS sorry, answered part of my own question. The stamps was public knowledge, so it&#39;s something he could have ran with, so to speak.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1700-->
<!--Post: 1714--><!--Time: 1102650185-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1714"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Esau<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Esau<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Have the police ever compared DNA evidence from BTK and The East Area Rapist/Original Night Stalker? Both operated in the same years and both are still making contact with either police, media or past victims. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1714-->
<!--Post: 1715--><!--Time: 1102653030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1715"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryan_olesin<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryan_olesin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 09, 2004 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Esau, I&#39;m not as familiar with EAR/ONS but what recent contact has he made?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1715-->
<!--Post: 1721--><!--Time: 1102667224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1721"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 10, 2004 - 12:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This, for example: <BR> <BR><i>&#34;His grandfather played the fiddle and died of a lung disease.&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>If this is a fact, I wonder how the authorities don&#39;t know BTK&#39;s name. This is not the best example I can select but it&#39;ll do.  <BR> <BR>There&#39;s a reason these facts were released. I don&#39;t know what the reason is, I only hope that the authorities aren&#39;t presenting information received from BTK as &#34;fact&#34; simply because BTK says it fact. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1721-->
<!--Post: 1725--><!--Time: 1102672277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1725"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 10, 2004 - 1:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The information provided by the BTK Strangler should not be interpreted as factual. Serial murderers who endeavor to communicate with the police or media organizations tend to craft codified messages. The messages tend to reflect fantasy and fact. It can be difficult to distinguish between the two. Providing information in this form is motivated by a desire to confuse the police and the public rather than reveal the identity of the unknown subject. It allows the BTK Strangler to exert  control and be manipulative. <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1725-->
<!--Post: 1732--><!--Time: 1102712676-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Shyra<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Shyra<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 10, 2004 - 1:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think this person acted on his worst fears.  I think he was trying to disprove his fears by doing what he did.   <BR> <BR>Maybe it sounds too good to be true but with all that passion involved, he knew he didn&#39;t imagine it and I guess he was just trying to reassure himself of his place in &#34;society. &#34; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1732-->
<!--Post: 1741--><!--Time: 1102730207-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1741"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 10, 2004 - 5:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I may be way off here or I could be on to something. I&#39;ll give you my theory on BTK&#39;s occupation.  <BR>First let&#39;s go back to the poem he wrote &#39;Oh Anna why didn&#39;t you appear.&#39; He talks of &#34;new vines at night...fresh spring rain...storm fury, winter calm...bed of spring moist grass.&#34; Looking at that terminology and the entire poem in itself it almost looks like it was written by a woman, not a man. Unless maybe you delt with nature, the outdoors and flora in your everyday life. Like a gardner. A landscaper.  <BR>Could BTK be a landscaper? The tools of the trade would make it easy for him to go undetected as a possibly suspect if stopped for a simple traffic citation. Here we would have gloves, ropes and twine of all varieties like cotton, hemp, nylon and clippers and tape and plastic bags of all sizes and even a tool tote bag. <BR>He would drive a van or a pickup truck. <BR>He would have a professional knowlege of tying knots. <BR>He would, if he ran his own business, have a portfollio of past projects to show when bidding on prospective new projects and they would be of photographs of landscaping he did for homes or business. Photographs he took himself. <BR>What about the mechanical engineering books used for concealing letters at the libray? A landscaper may indeed have a familiarity of mechanical engineering if they are installing or maintaining sprinkler systems, water pumps, piping and drainage systems. <BR>I read somewhere that in the BTK self profile where he mentions the names Tina and Petra that someone noted that there were the names Christina and Petra engraved in the bricks of the Plaza of Heroines at the WSU campus. That was a landscaped project. Did BTK work on that project&#39;s landscaping? Did he learn landscaping through classes at WSU? Did he learn landscaping while serving time in prison? Did he work for someone or have his own business? A landscaper would be an early riser and have flexible off hours throughout the day. Was BTK a landscaper? Maybe he still is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1741-->
<!--Post: 1756--><!--Time: 1102806639-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1756"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 11, 2004 - 3:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Determining the occupations of serial murderers can be difficult. Ted Bundy was a social worker, Michael Ross became an insurance salesman after studying agricultural economics at Cornell University, Ed Kemper was employed in the public sector with the California Division of Highways and David Allen Lucas was a carpet cleaner. The BTK Strangler could be a garden landscaper, a mechanic, repaired electrical equipment, a small business owner, employed by the public sector or the corporate world. His occupation would have to provide him with autonomy and flexibility. It would allow him to commit murders without anyone noticing his actions. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1756-->
<!--Post: 1772--><!--Time: 1102828696-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1772"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 11, 2004 - 9:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whatever his occupation may have been or still is I also think he worked within the circle of the killings linked to him. Maybe not necessarily lived within those perimiters but worked there and could get in and out quickly and confidently.  <BR>When BTK asked victim Kevin Bright &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34; I don&#39;t think it conclusively implied that BTK was a student taking classes there but may have done work for an extended period of time on the WSU campus.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1772-->
<!--Post: 1810--><!--Time: 1102902114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 5:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In reference to Pat Brown&#39;s most current info/profile, does anyone know if those traits were gleaned from the police or are they her speculations based on experience? I assume that they are her deductions. If BTK is a non-secretor, he is predisposed to a large number of diseases/medical conditions over a nonsecretor. His biology will come into play and cramp his style. Perhaps that is why he is apparently less active, if that is the word to be used. FYI, for what it is worth: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.dadamo.com/napharm/store3/template2/secretor.htm" target=_top>http://www.dadamo.com/napharm/store3/template2/sec retor.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1810-->
<!--Post: 1812--><!--Time: 1102918784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1812"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 10:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The BTK Strangler and other serial murderers who communicate with the police tend to use semiotics to manipulate them and the public. This method increases the likelihood of the BTK Strangler enjoying freedom. An example could be the reference to Petra. Petra could be an acquaintance, a former student at Wichita State University or a woman the unknown subject desired from a distance or she may have rejected his affection. Another example could be his relationship with Wichita State University. The unknown subject may have studied at the university, he may have been employed by the institution as an academic or was required to repair equipment in the library. Semiotics tend to enrich language, but in the context of criminology it increases the ambiguity. Considerable evidence has to be gathered to ascertain the validity of statements made by the BTK Strangler.    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1812-->
<!--Post: 1813--><!--Time: 1102919571-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1813"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 10:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d like this thread to stay specific to Mike Kelleher&#39;s profile of BTK. However, if someone wants to start a thread about other profiles, feel free.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1813-->
<!--Post: 1833--><!--Time: 1102985191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1833"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Several factors would have compelled the BTK Strangler to engage with the police and the media this year. It seems he currently enjoys greater freedom. It seems unlikely recent unemployment or retirement rekindled his interest in asserting control and domination over the police and public. A divorce or the death of his wife would have compelled him. His children would have left home in recent years and he is alone and can again concentrate on his primary passion. <BR> <BR>Robert Beattie&#39;s book on the BTK Strangler could have been the catalyst. He would be infuriated someone would contemplate such a project without his approval. His anger could be attributed to the belief Beattie was not as accomplished as he is. The unknown subject believes he possesses superior intelligence to Beattie, the police and the public. The unknown subject believes he is the only one who could adequately accomplish this task. Secondly, Beattie could profit from it and the BTK Strangler will not receive a cent.  <BR> <BR>The unknown subject would have found it difficult to restrain his desire to murder and the enjoyment derived from strangulation or inflicting fatal wounds on a victim. It would be difficult for him to repress the desires for almost twenty years. He most probably murdered a few more women during the last decade. The pleasure derived from murder is akin to sexual gratification for the BTK Strangler. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1833-->
<!--Post: 1898--><!--Time: 1103084105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 8:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Michael D. Keleher has been proven correct in his profile of BTK in saying he will be taking caculated risks. Sending a drivers license belonging to a murder victim from 18 years ago is about as bizarre as it gets until he leaves to be found a drivers license from a murder victim of 27 years ago. Kelleher and all profilers might want to reevaluate their profiles on BTK. This is a whole new breed of cat.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1898-->
